The more I study Midnight Network, the less I think this is only a privacy story. It feels more like a trust shift. Selective disclosure is the obvious strength: sensitive data stays off-chain, while settlement stays public and auditable. That is a real fit for compliance-heavy sectors. But the risk does not disappear. It moves into setup governance, proof systems, witness code, and early centralized controls. So the real question is not whether trust is reduced. It is where that trust now lives.
